<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32576" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnĭpărens</span></b> ,
		tis, adj.
		omnis-parens, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>all-bearing</i>, <i>all-producing</i>
				(<b>poet.</b> and in post-class. prose); so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per terras omniparentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 706</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 595</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">App. M. 6, p. 177, 24</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dea Syria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 8</span></i>
			, p. 213, 9 (but in <i><span class="en">id. Mund. p. 67,
			12</span></i>, the correct read. is omnia parentis).</div>
